  "exp.envDetectedHtml": "Detected environment: <strong>{system}</strong> · shell <code>{shell}</code>",
  "exp.envUserHtml": "user <code>{user}</code>",
  "exp.mcp.step1Html": "Create a token at <a href=\"{page}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">kaggle.com/settings</a> → <em>Account</em> tab → <em>API</em> section → <em>Generate New Token</em> (it starts with <code>KGAT_</code>).",
  "exp.mcp.step2Html": "Press <strong>Activate</strong>: it opens the dashboard's smith CLI assistant and runs {command}. Paste the token in the terminal (the input stays hidden); smith checks it against Kaggle and saves it for your user only in {path}{perms}, the same file the official Kaggle CLI and SDK use, never inside the project. If you already had another token there, add <code>--replace</code>.",
  "exp.mcp.perms": " (permissions 0600)",
  "exp.mcp.step3Html": "Open a new Claude, OpenCode or Pi session from the assistant: the dashboard passes it {env} and the <code>kaggle</code> MCP is authenticated. Outside the dashboard, in your shell: {export}; to keep it in every new session, add that line to {profile}.",
  "exp.mcp.step4Html": "Check with {command} (it reads your weekly GPU quota); <code>smith mcp kaggle deactivate</code> deletes the token.",
