  "exp.colab.title": "Connect Google Colab (CLI and MCP)",
  "exp.colab.officialHtml": "Official MCP <code>{server}</code>: {registered}.",
  "exp.colab.step1Html": "Install the official Colab CLI at the pinned version: {command}.",
  "exp.colab.step2Html": "Each team member registers their own account: {command}. Replace <code>&lt;slug&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;Name&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;tier&gt;</code> (<code>free</code>, {tiers}) in the terminal: the button types the command without running it.",
  "exp.colab.step3Html": "Each person signs in with their own account in the CLI assistant: {command}. The CLI's state stays in <code>~/.config/papersmith/colab/&lt;slug&gt;/</code> (permissions 0700); papersmith never reads or copies those files.",
  "exp.colab.step4Html": "Check with {status}; {list} shows the team.",
  "exp.colab.step5Html": "Colab's official MCP is for interactive work: it needs a Colab notebook open in the browser, which the agent (Claude, OpenCode or Pi) connects to. Headless runs go through the CLI and <code>/remote-execution</code>.",
  "exp.colab.teamRule": "Team rule",
  "exp.colab.rule1Html": "One account per person and service. The <a href=\"{faq}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Colab FAQ</a> does not allow \"using multiple accounts to work around access or resource usage restrictions\" and, in free environments without compute units, \"running distributed computing workers\".",
  "exp.colab.rule2Html": "That is why Colab campaigns run only on paid tiers ({tiers}); a <code>free</code> account serves for the interactive proof of concept in one session, never as a worker of a split campaign.",
  "exp.colab.rule3": "Parallelism counts distinct people, not accounts.",
